# LangGraph Patterns

## Graph structure
- One graph per SDLC stage. Each graph has typed state 
  (Pydantic model in `state.py`).
- Standard node set: `retrieve` → `plan` → `execute` → `self_review` → 
  `output_validate`. Use conditional edges for replan loops (bounded).
- Every graph exposes `.ainvoke(state) -> state`. Called from a 
  Temporal Activity.

## State
- State is fully serializable (Pydantic). No live connections, no file 
  handles. Serialize into `agent_activity` result payload for Temporal 
  to persist in workflow history.
- Include `trace_id`, `run_id`, `stage_id`, `parent_workflow_id` in every 
  state object for cross-system correlation.

## Prompts
- Load via `prompt_loader.get(name, version=None)`. LangSmith Hub is 
  canonical; falls back to `/prompts/*.md` on failure.
- Never inline long prompts in code.

## Tools
- Tools are Pydantic-typed. Every tool call is logged as an audit event.
- File-write tools MUST route through the policy engine before execution.

## Replanning
- Conditional edges may loop back to `plan` with an incremented 
  `replan_count`. Cap at 3. On exhaustion, raise `ReplanExhausted` — 
  Temporal workflow catches and escalates to HITL.

## LangSmith
- Every graph invocation is a LangSmith run. Set `metadata` with 
  `workflow_id`, `stage`, `scenario_type`.